  - created_at: "2026-11-21T02:45:49.891Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: Greptile discussion r4650110264 on 9a47c8c found a false refusal on an unrelated smoke script. The paired fixture first reproduced that refusal in both a package script and an unrelated workflow step. It also requires refusal when the configured changelog hook forwards into that script. Scope the generated-file rule to the existing release context and rerun the gates.
  - created_at: "2026-11-21T02:48:33.761Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Round FL follow-up maps PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M66QqFm to f00d119. The generated-file rule from 02ddd0b now follows the audited release context, including a configured hook forwarding into the tested smoke script. The same stand-alone smoke script and an unrelated workflow step pass. Paired controls, the date verifier and the pinned 142-hook and 144-body fleet scan passed. Focused and full release gates are running on the scoped fix."
  - created_at: "2026-11-21T03:07:09.530Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Round FL follow-up f00d119 passed all 349 focused tests, the paired scoped refusal and acceptance tests, typecheck, test build, lint, duplication, docstring, date audit, and a byte-identical changelog regeneration. The fleet accepted all 142 hooks and 144 bodies. At the pre-cutoff checkpoint, standalone coverage and rewritten acceptance were still running. Pushed head 9a47c8c passed CI and CodeQL, with the Greptile scope finding tracked above."
  - created_at: "2026-11-21T03:53:22.637Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Round FM started. Verify the thirteen review findings on the current release branch, exercise earlier refusals and valid hook forms, and compare the fleet fixture before recording gate results."
  - created_at: "2026-11-21T04:09:17.463Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Round FM red fixtures failed on the original review head for nine targeted cases. The current branch already contains the scoped inherited-binding checks. The workspace fixture checks opposing member, root, user and environment settings. A copied Node executable exercises a spaced path on POSIX too. The prototype corpus accepted all 142 configured hooks and 144 reached bodies."
  - created_at: "2026-11-21T04:16:46.563Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Round FM thread map for PR #295, verified against starting head 22f8352. Commit 6446306 addresses all thirteen PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M66P- threads. 56 preserves expression-valued environment uncertainty. 59 limits definite environment writes to recognized executing shell templates. 6D documents the hook-options check. 6F classifies tee destinations. 6K refuses alternate custom notes renderers while accepting an unconditional final renderer or prepared generator branches. 6N consumes the lexer-decoded here-document delimiters with physical edit offsets. 6P preserves the selected JSON and step-output path. 6W uses the active npm configuration loader and records unknown when unresolved. 6X re-detects the verified project for empty and absent legacy receipt values. 6f accepts timeout -p. 6l copies Node to a spaced executable path and exercises the .exe entry point. 6o verifies the next untagged version heading. 6r sets one explicit lifecycle environment for preparation and real npm execution. Prior binding threads 650IRm and 650SdF are covered by 24d844c and rechecked with the current code."
  - created_at: "2026-11-21T04:38:20.938Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "The direct reference suite identified one fixture integration failure among 1355 tests. The isolated empty-probe checkout omitted the lifecycle helper imported by continuation. Include that source in the fixture closure, retaining the no-node_modules and no-npm-invocation assertions."
  - created_at: "2026-11-21T05:01:35.820Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "The 29 direct-reference files passed with 1472 passes and two opt-in skips after the fixture closure fix in f7502f4. Standalone coverage passed all test assertions but measured one unexecuted static npmrc branch. Add explicit refusal for unrelated settings alone and acceptance for an unrelated key preceding a literal lifecycle setting, then repeat both coverage gates."
